On Sunday, September 1, 2013 9:45:29 AM UTC-4, Dominic Edwards wrote:
>
> 1: How can I fix one element from a vector of parameter?
>
>
>
> Initially I tried (attached as ToyModel1.stan) :
> transformed parameters{
> ...
> vector[NT] Beta;
> Beta[1] <- 0;
> ...
> }

You want to declare the free elements in the parameters section and then copy them into a larger vector in the model section after specifying the fixed values. Then put the prior on the former. Like this

parameters {
  vector[NT-1] Beta_free;
}
model {
  vector[NT] Beta;
  Beta[1] <- 0.0;
  for (i in 1:(NT-1)) Beta[i+1] <- Beta_free[i];
  Beta_free <- normal(0.0, 4.0);
  ...
}

In the next version of Stan, there is a tail() function which would allow you to write this without the explicit loop in the .stan file but either way it becomes a fast loop in the C++ code.

Ben

