From ud00f6178fa8e05fe at groups.google.com  Wed Sep  4 14:52:59 2013
From: ud00f6178fa8e05fe at groups.google.com (=?utf-8?b?TWFydGluIMWgbcOtcmE=?=)
Date: Wed, 04 Sep 2013 14:52:59 +0000
Subject: wrong mixing
Message-ID: <PF12DT7DKRU.FIVmky2eSJAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/PF12DT7DKRU/m/FIVmky2eSJAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I'm trying to fit a model with categorical distribution sampling. I have it wokring on JAGS, but couldn't fit it in Stan.
Any suggestions about what's going wrong? Am I incrementing log posterior in the right way? Is it even possible to fit this model in Stan?
 It goes like this:

 <https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/-3EB7EQOyVL0/UidBT6n-FDI/AAAAAAAAAJM/LWlmrGFOANU/s1600/model.jpg>
JAGS code: model{
  for (i in 1:m){
     k[i] ~ dbin(theta,n)
  }
  theta ~ dbeta(1,1)
  n ~ dcat(p[])
  for (i in 1:nmax){
    p[i] <- 1/nmax
  }}
Description of example:
There are five helpers distributing a bundle of surveys to houses. It is known that each bundle contained the same number of surveys, n, but the number itself is not known. The only available relevant information is that the maximum bundle is Nmax = 500, and so n must be between 1 and Nmax. (https://webfiles.uci.edu/mdlee/BB_Free.pdf, page 51)

My RStan code:
model ="
data {
  int nmax;
  int m;
  int k[m];
  int n[nmax];
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0,upper=1> theta;
  simplex[nmax] mix;
}
model {
  real ps[nmax];
  theta ~ beta(1, 1);

  for (i in 1:m) {
    for (j in 1:nmax) {
      ps[j] <- log(mix[j]) + binomial_log(k[i], n[j], theta);
    }
    lp__ <- lp__ + log_sum_exp(ps);
  }
}"

k <- c(16, 18, 22, 25, 27)
m <- length(k)
n <- seq(max(k),500,by=1)
nmax <- length(n)

data <- list(k=k, m=m, nmax=nmax, n=n) # to be passed on to Stan

sa=sample(1:10,nmax,replace=T)
sa=sa/sum(sa)
sb=sample(1:10,nmax,replace=T)
sb=sa/sum(sa)
sc=sample(1:10,nmax,replace=T)
sc=sa/sum(sa)

myinits <- list(
  list(theta=runif(1), mix=sa),
  list(theta=runif(1), mix=sb),
  list(theta=runif(1), mix=sc))

# parameters to be monitored:
parameters <- c("theta")

samples <- stan(model_code=model,
                data=data,
                init=myinits,
#                pars=parameters,
                iter=1000,
                chains=3,
                thin=1)

RESULTS
JAGS results:

 <https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-IkFj0pccUaI/UidFM7f15rI/AAAAAAAAAJY/zVa3p14zUIU/s1600/result+JAGS.jpg>

Stan results:
 <https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-soDFBxGImXo/UidIhjdGUzI/AAAAAAAAAJk/Gxf4V4yDhP8/s1600/result+Stan.jpeg>Mixing is flat. Theta varies from 0 to 0.1

Thank you,

Martin Smira

