Yes, you can fit mixture models in Stan.

I don't quite understand your model, but it looks
fishy --- there are only four data points (m=4)
being used to fit a 500-dimensional mixture.

And it doesn't look like the translation of the JAGS model.

I would expect the number of outcome counts (your k)
to match the number of trial counts (your n), but
it doesn't.  Here's what I see in your data:

