There are certainly some problems where the performance of HMC is known to drop, but the variation in run times is far more indicative of problems with our adaptation routines during warmup.  When a chain starts way out in a tail the adaptation can be too aggressive and lead to poor sampling.  Try running with tighter initialization values -- on the develop branch you can specify init=x to produce random values between [-x, x].

