Dear Stan users,

Thanks for the feedback. First off, yes, when you assume large measurement error the convergence for sigma becomes problematic; in fact, we have started to look in to this just last week (a coincidence; Martin was unaware of this). The convergence problems may arise because of model misspecification (the data were not generated with large measurement error; instead, the were generated with no measurement error, and then the amount of measurement error was simply assumed to be present). The convergence problem is also present in WinBUGS.

Thanks for all the other suggestions for improvement

Cheers,
E.J.

