I'm a learner, I'm trying to rewrite from BUGS to STAN the models from
the ARM book, so I've looked at the book by Lee & Wagenmakers too.

The example about Cha Sa-soon (ï¿½5.5) is really amusing, but it could
also be interesting (and eventually not so easy to rewrite) because:
a) one can't pass a vector such as z <- c(rep(NA, 949), 30) to Stan;
b) the censored data can be treated as missing data (Stan Manual, ï¿½9.2,
p. 44), but one can't define parameters such as

int<lower=15,upper=25> z[N_cens];

because:
(i) the error message I got said that integer parameters are not allowed;
(ii) the binomial() function requires an integer lhs.

So after looking at "Integrating out Censored Values" (Manual, p. 45)
I've tried:

data{
   int<lower=0> N_cens;     // 949
   int<lower=0> n;     // 50
   int<lower=0> z_obs;     // 30
}
parameters {
   real<lower=0.25,upper=1.0> p;
}
model {
   z_obs ~ binomial(n, p);
   lp__ <- lp__ + N_cens *
                  log(binomial_cdf(25, n, p) - binomial_cdf(14, n, p));
}

My results look reassuring:

 > print(chasasoon.sf, probs=c(0.025,0.5,0.975), digits=2)
...
         mean se_mean  sd    2.5%     50%   97.5% n_eff Rhat
p       0.40    0.00 0.0    0.39    0.40    0.41  1871    1
lp__ -152.26    0.03 0.7 -154.62 -151.97 -151.75   489    1

I hope this helps... if I'm right.
I hope someone helps me if I'm wrong ;-)

Sergio

