Cool --- that's one observation of 30 and N_cens observations of an
unknown value in a known range.

We really need to get the following functions for each density
FOO built in:

   g_FOO(x,y,theta) = log(FOO_cdf(x,theta) - FOO_cdf(y,theta))

We use it in actual truncation models, too, and it's not
the most arithmetically stable way to implement the function,
nor the most efficient given the shared parameters theta and
the use of auto-diff to do all the derivatives.

