> > several elements from a Dirichlet() distribution. I've attached the model and dataset and have used a development
> > version from Marcus to be able to access the matrix_normal distribution. The question is how to correct lp__ for the
> > logit transformation / change of variables? I understand a simple example (e.g. the logit transformation of a scalar,
> > similar to several examples in the manual), but here I have a full matrix and a summation, and I'm not sure how the
> > correction works in such a case. Perhaps someone with better math-skills than me can help out (!), thanks in advance.
