issue, e.g., I would estimate one coefficient for the average effect
of X2 by race, r(i)*X2 in the notation I've been using, and then I
would estimate differences around that by group h, where I would
assume, or allow the model to estimate, that such variation was
smaller than the variation between, e.g., r(1)*X2 and r(3)*X1.

To be more concrete about what I was thinking, the model would have
beta[i, k] coefficient for race x covariate, with beta[i, k] ~
normal(0, sd1)
sd1
and
gamma[i, j, k] coefficients for the interaction, distributed normal(0, sd2),
so the total effect for i,j, k = beta[i, k] + gamma[i, j, k]

where I suspect that sd2 < sd1.

