But end up explicitly looping:
data {
  matrix[3,3] X;
}
parameters {
  matrix[3,3] mu;
  matrix[3,3] sigma;
}
model {
  for (row in 1:3) {
    for (col in 1:3) {
      X[row, col] ~ normal(mu[row,col], sigma[row,col]);
      mu[row, col] ~ normal(0, 1);
      sigma[row, col] ~ inv_gamma(6, 5);
    }
  }
}

Since there is
normal_log(real[1], vector, vector) : real
could one get
normal_log(real[1], matrix, matrix) : real

BR,
Henrik

