Just to clarify, the change I made was not from fixed to random effects,
though it is perhaps analogous one level up.  A simplified version is
the change from
sigma ~ cauchy(0, 5)
beta ~ normal(0, 5)
y ~ normal(beta*x, sigma)

to

sigma ~ cauchy(0, 5)
sigma2 ~ cauchy(0, 5)
beta ~ normal(0, sigma2)
y ~ normal(beta*x, sigma)

The estimated sigma2 was around 0.1

Ross

