I found exactly that same behavior with an IRT model I was fitting.

Trying to write a Bayesian model to approximate the usual
MLE model required some fiddling with hand-coded priors to identify
the model.  Putting a hyperprior on the items and abilities (and
adding an intercept so that items and abilities could be centered
around 0) solved  the problem right away.

I should write this up in the manual.

The simplification part is more just to understand the model
by building up from working pieces until you hit something
that doesn't work.

- Bob

