I think we talked about cauchy(0,5) at one point.

Your Bayesian Analysis paper uses a Cauchy scale of 25 for
a std dev parameter (see figure 2).

   http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/taumain.pdf

For regression coefficients, your paper in Ann. Appl. Stat. suggests
a scale of 2.5:

   http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/priors11.pdf

There you assume (see abstract) that all parameters are translated
and scaled to have mean 0 and std dev 0.5.  If they were
standardized  (mean 0 and std dev 1), wouldn't cauchy(0,5) amount to the
same thing?  (But I really do remember seeing cauchy(0,5) on your
board --- but then I might have written it there misremembering the 2.5
or 25 numbers.)

- Bob

