So the Omega[2,2] isn't exactly 1.0, so the R-hat doesn't become NaN.

> all the other Rhats are 1, I guess is because it is in the diagaonal of the correlation matrix, but for the other elements of the diagonla I get Rhat=1. I dont think this is a problem, but is weird.

Exactly.  And we need to figure out an appropriate fix
for that issue.  The problem as the code stands is that
we don't distinguish among the different types of matrices
in the I/O code.

