Aah, yes, these are 2 different Cauchys.  But the 25 in the  Cauchy (0, 25) example came from substantive concenrs, it's not a default value.

On Sep 30, 2013, at 1:11 AM, Bob Carpenter wrote:

> I think we talked about cauchy(0,5) at one point.
>
> Your Bayesian Analysis paper uses a Cauchy scale of 25 for
> a std dev parameter (see figure 2).
>
>  http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/taumain.pdf
>
> For regression coefficients, your paper in Ann. Appl. Stat. suggests
> a scale of 2.5:
>
>  http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/priors11.pdf
